node_modules/
# ...except the ones that are test data. WP21 S1 derives a module's package
# from the `node_modules/<name>` directory it sits in, so the fixture for two
# packages compiling together has to be laid out the way npm lays one out.
!tests/link/*/node_modules/
dist/
build/
web/*.wasm
*.o
*.s
*.bc
a.out
.claude/worktrees/

# tests/link/no_main is a negative case: the compiler writes the IR beside the
# source before it reports the missing `main`, so every run of the link section
# leaves this behind. Two .ll files under tests/link ARE checked in
# (two_file/), so this names the one that leaks rather than ignoring the glob.
tests/link/no_main/main.ll
